DAY 5

Customer Service Production Enhancements

Enterprise Financial Data Platform

Objective: harden the Customer Service persistence layer and API behavior using production-style database migrations, Oracle-generated identifiers, pagination/search/filtering, transaction boundaries, validation, duplicate handling, and regression testing.

1. Day 5 Architecture

REST API -> DTO Validation -> Controller -> Service (@Transactional)
         -> Repository / Specifications -> JPA / Hibernate
         -> Oracle

Flyway -> Versioned DDL/DML -> Oracle Schema
Oracle Trigger + Sequence -> 6-digit CUSTOMER_NUMBER

2. Production Database Ownership

Hibernate schema generation remains disabled with spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=none.

Flyway owns database schema evolution. JPA/Hibernate maps to the schema and performs normal business CRUD.

Flyway DML is used only for controlled bootstrap/migration data, not normal customer transactions.

Customer numbers are generated by Oracle rather than Java.

The 6-character VARCHAR2 customer number preserves leading zeros such as 000001.

