6. Oracle-Generated Customer Number

The old Java System.currentTimeMillis()-based CUST number generation was removed. The repository method existsByCustomerNumber() was also removed because it is no longer needed for generation.

Entity mapping:

@Column(
        name = "CUSTOMER_NUMBER",
        nullable = false,
        length = 6,
        insertable = false,
        updatable = false
)
private String customerNumber;

After an INSERT, CustomerService flushes the SQL and refreshes the managed entity so the API can return the value generated by the Oracle trigger.

Customer savedCustomer = customerRepository.saveAndFlush(customer);
entityManager.refresh(savedCustomer);
return CustomerMapper.toResponse(savedCustomer);

7. Customer Status Hardening

public enum CustomerStatus {
    ACTIVE,
    INACTIVE
}

Entity mapping uses EnumType.STRING:

@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
@Column(name = "CUSTOMER_STATUS", nullable = false, length = 20)
private CustomerStatus customerStatus;

The database also enforces CK_CUSTOMERS_STATUS, allowing only ACTIVE and INACTIVE. Application-level enum validation and database-level constraints provide complementary protection.

