11. Validation and Exception Handling

DTO validation covers required names/email, email format, phone format, date of birth, and field sizes.

Page and size parameters use @Min/@Max validation.

Invalid sort fields/directions return HTTP 400.

CustomerNotFoundException returns HTTP 404.

DuplicateCustomerException returns HTTP 409.

DataIntegrityViolationException provides database-level conflict protection.

ConstraintViolationException and MethodArgumentNotValidException return HTTP 400.

12. Issues Encountered and Resolved

Issue

Resolution

Flyway checksum mismatch

V1/V2 had previously been applied with different contents. Because this was local development and the baseline was intentionally rebuilt, the old local schema/history was reset rather than hiding the mismatch.

Failed V1 migration

Oracle created CUSTOMERS and CUSTOMER_NUMBER_SEQ but failed before creating the trigger. Flyway correctly recorded V1 as failed.

CREATE TRIGGER privilege

financial_user did not have CREATE TRIGGER. The privilege was granted from the SYSTEM connection, partial V1 objects/history were cleaned, and Flyway was rerun from a clean local state.

Quoted Flyway history table

The Flyway history table was addressed using its actual Oracle/Flyway name: "flyway_schema_history".

Enum search

The free-text repository query previously attempted LOWER(customerStatus). After CustomerStatus became an enum, status was removed from generic text search and kept as a dedicated filter.

