14. Key Engineering Lessons

Never silently edit already-applied production migrations. Day 5 rebaselining was acceptable only because this was an intentionally reset local development schema.

Schema migration ownership and business-data ownership are different concerns: Flyway evolves schema; repositories/services perform runtime CRUD.

Database-generated values require ORM mapping that does not attempt to insert/update the generated column, plus a mechanism to read the generated value back.

Application validation should not replace database constraints; both protect different boundaries.

A production-style service needs more than CRUD: pagination limits, safe sorting, transactions, predictable errors, constraints, observability and repeatable migrations all matter.

